Statement: "Because the publish ran inside the transaction callback, the failed COMMIT also withdraws enrollment.created from the broker, so no consumer will process an event for enr_70318."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. Only operations that go through tx take part in the PostgreSQL transaction. The broker acknowledged the message at .219, so it is in the broker''s log, and a rollback in PostgreSQL has no way to remove it. Consumers will process an event for an enrollment that was rolled back: a ghost event. Publishing inside the callback is really the order publish-then-commit, and it adds two more problems: the transaction (with its locks and pooled connection) stays open during a network call, and a broker outage now blocks every enrollment. The misconception is that code placed inside a transaction callback is automatically transactional.', 2, 5
