Statement: "The commit and the publish are two independent writes; for 37 requests the publish failed after COMMIT had already made the enrollment durable, and the catch block turned each lost event into a 201."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. This is the dual write in order A (commit, then publish). The COMMIT is durable on its own; the publish is a second write to another system, and nothing ties the two together. During the failover the publish timed out, the catch logged a warning and returned, and the controller answered 201, so neither the learner nor any alert noticed. The 37 warnings in C match the 37 missing receipts in B. The misconception is that logging an error is handling it: after the catch, nothing remembers that the event still has to be sent.', 2, 5
