Statement: "Because the outbox row commits together with the enrollment, the relay publishes every event exactly once, so the certificate service can stop deduplicating by event id."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The outbox closes the gap in the request (the event can no longer be lost or exist without its row), but the relay has its own gap: a crash, a timeout or a lost acknowledgement after the publish and before the UPDATE leaves the row pending, and the next tick publishes it again. The outbox gives at-least-once delivery. It is safe because the message id is the outbox row id, so the copy carries the same id and a consumer that deduplicates by event id processes it once. Removing the deduplication would send a second welcome email after the next relay crash. The misconception is that "transactional" on the producer side means exactly-once delivery end to end.', 5, 5
