INSERT INTO challenge.challenges (public_id, course_id, module_id, lesson_id, name, title, description, status, difficulty, type, points, is_published, is_deleted)
VALUES ('chal_coding_dce_412', (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'data-consistency-events'), (SELECT id FROM course.module WHERE course_id = (SELECT id FROM catalog.course WHERE public_id = 'data-consistency-events') AND order_index = 4 AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), (SELECT id FROM course.lesson WHERE content_source = 'lesson-dce-4-1' AND is_deleted = false LIMIT 1), 'saga-buy-premium-course', 'An orchestrated saga with compensation and resume', 'Buying a premium course on CodeDev touches four services: pay (reserve points or charge the card), enroll, grant (the entitlement that unlocks the lessons) and receipt (the email). Write the seven actions and the orchestrator runSaga so that a failed step is undone by compensations in reverse order, every action can be retried, and a crash at any point resumes correctly from the saga record stored in the database. key = "<userId>:<courseId>". ACTIONS: each runs in one transaction on the copy t of the tables and must be idempotent (running it again after it committed changes nothing). pay: if payments already has the sagaId, do nothing; for method "points", balance = wallets[userId] (0 when missing): if balance < price throw BusinessError("insufficient points"), else subtract the price; then set payments[sagaId] = { userId, method, amount: price, status: "captured" } (for "card" the card network is simulated by the scripted faults). enroll: an active enrollment for the key of the same saga: do nothing; active and of another saga: throw BusinessError("already enrolled"); otherwise set { sagaId, status: "active" }. grant: set entitlements[key] = { sagaId, active: true }. receipt: if receipts has an entry for the sagaId do nothing, else push { sagaId, userId, amount: price }. refund: only when payments[sagaId] exists and is "captured": mark it "refunded" and, for points, add the amount back to wallets[userId]. cancelEnrollment: only when enrollments[key] belongs to this saga and is active: set "cancelled". revokeEntitlement: only when entitlements[key] belongs to this saga and is active: set active false. Compensations never throw: nothing to undo means do nothing. runSaga(ctx, order): load the record; if there is none, an order is valid when method is "points" or "card" and price is a positive integer: save { order, status: "running", done: [], undone: [], error: null }, or for an invalid order save status "aborted" with error "invalid order" and run nothing. Every action goes through ctx.perform(action, order), at most ctx.maxAttempts calls in a row: TransientError: call again; BusinessError: stop, the reason is its message; maxAttempts transient errors: the reason is "gave up after <maxAttempts> attempts"; let a Crash (and any other error) propagate. Status "running": run pay, enroll, grant in this order, skipping steps already in done; after each success push it to done and save; on a failure set status "compensating" and error "<step>: <reason>", save, then compensate. After grant, send the receipt: on success push "receipt" to done, status "completed", error null; on failure status "receipt_pending" and error "receipt: <reason>" - the purchase is NOT compensated; save. Compensate (status "compensating" or "stuck"): for the steps in done in reverse order run refund for pay, cancelEnrollment for enroll, revokeEntitlement for grant, skipping those already in undone; push each success to undone and save; when one still fails after maxAttempts calls set status "stuck" (keep the error), save and stop; when all succeeded set status "aborted" and save. Status "receipt_pending": retry the receipt as above. "completed" and "aborted": do nothing. The runner reads { maxAttempts, wallets, enrollments?, orders, faults?, crashes?, rerun? }. faults[sagaId][action] scripts the calls of perform in order: "transient" throws TransientError before anything is written, "fail:<reason>" throws BusinessError(reason) (for a compensation it counts as transient), "ok" or no entry runs your action in a transaction. crashes "<sagaId>:<action>#<n>": the process dies right after the n-th successful run of that action commits; the runner then calls runSaga again for that order with a fresh context (memory is lost, the database is kept). With rerun, after all orders the runner calls runSaga once more per order. It prints the call log, every saga record and the tables. Do not change the types, FakeDb, the errors, the context or the runner.', 'open', 'hard'::difficulty_question, 'mini_coding', 40, true, false)
