INSERT INTO challenge.challenge_hints (challenge_id, level, body)
VALUES ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_dce_412'), 1, 'After a crash, the only thing your next run knows is the saga record in the database. For every place where the process can die - after an action committed but before you saved, or between two compensations - ask: what does the record say, what will runSaga do with it, and what happens if it runs that same action a second time?'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_dce_412'), 2, 'Three places decide most tests. In the forward loop, save status "compensating" with the error BEFORE the first compensation runs, or a resume goes forward again. In compensate, walk done backwards and skip what is already in undone. In the actions, check the current row first (payments.has, payment status "captured", enrollment owned by this saga and active, receipt already sent) so a second run is a no-op.'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_dce_412'), 3, 'A similar flow with different steps: a ticket booking reserves a seat, then charges, then emails. If charge fails, the record { done: [reserve], status: "compensating" } is saved and releaseSeat runs. If the process dies right after releaseSeat committed, the next run reads the same record, runs releaseSeat again - it finds the seat already free and does nothing - pushes it to undone and ends "aborted". If the email fails three times, the booking stands with status "email_pending" and a later run sends only the email.');
