outbox_pending_rows                 118     (normal on weekdays: 80-150)
outbox_oldest_pending_age_seconds   9612

outbox-publisher 13:59:55 WARN publish failed id=ob_771203 type=LessonCompleted error="record too large" attempt=1922
outbox-publisher 13:59:55 INFO published batch size=100 skipped=1

Statement: "An alert on the pending row count would stay silent here, while an alert on the oldest pending age set at 5 minutes would fire."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. Because the publisher skips the failing row, the rest of the queue drains and the count stays inside its normal range, so a count threshold has nothing to see. The oldest pending age measures how long the slowest waiting event has already waited: 9,612 s is more than two and a half hours, far above 300 s. That row is a real learner''s LessonCompleted event, so their progress, leaderboard points and possibly certificate are stuck. The misconception is that a normal-looking backlog means a healthy outbox; the count describes traffic, the age describes waiting.', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_dce_521') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
)
